From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/ems: switch core sparing per emstune set

The S5E9965 EMS sets the minimum active cpus per emstune set (ECS dynamic).
The Exynos 990 has the ECS governor (sparing.c) but no DT node, so it never
ran. Add the node with a saving mode on cpus 0-5, which keeps tasks off the
Mongoose cluster until all six little/mid cpus are busy, and let each set
turn it on with an ecs node. Sets without one inherit the mode's default
set. emstune_ecs_apply() runs on every set change; ecs_emstune_update()
keeps the request until init_core_sparing() is ready, since both are late
initcalls. /sys/kernel/ems/emstune/ecs_enabled disables it at runtime.

Normal, power-scenario and light-video spare the Mongoose cores in their
default and med boost sets; touch and big boost (input, app launch) and
every other mode keep all cpus.
---
--- a/kernel/sched/ems/sparing.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/ems/sparing.c
@@ -300,6 +300,22 @@
 ecs_mode_store(mode_enabled, enabled);
 ecs_mode_show(mode_enabled, enabled);
 
+/*
+ * emstune turns the governor on and off per set. Its requests can arrive
+ * before init_core_sparing() (both are late initcalls) or when the DT has no
+ * ECS node; keep the last one and apply it once the governor is ready.
+ */
+static bool ecs_ready;
+static bool ecs_emstune_enabled;
+static int ecs_set_enable(bool enable);
+
+void ecs_emstune_update(bool enable)
+{
+	WRITE_ONCE(ecs_emstune_enabled, enable);
+	if (READ_ONCE(ecs_ready))
+		ecs_set_enable(enable);
+}
+
 static int ecs_set_enable(bool enable)
 {
 	struct ecs_mode *base_mode = ecs_get_base_mode();
@@ -648,7 +664,10 @@
 	if (ecs_sysfs_init())
 		goto failure;
 
-	ecs_gov.enabled = 1;
+	/* Start in the base mode; emstune decides whether to spare cpus. */
+	ecs_set_enable(true);
+	WRITE_ONCE(ecs_ready, true);
+	ecs_set_enable(READ_ONCE(ecs_emstune_enabled));
 
 	return 0;
 
--- a/kernel/sched/ems/ems.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/ems/ems.h
@@ -128,6 +128,7 @@
 
 /* core sparing */
 extern struct cpumask *ecs_cpus_allowed(void);
